(d) Safety instruction. All employees shall be instructed in the recognition
and avoidance of hazards associated with underground construction
activities including, where appropriate, the following subjects:
(1) Air monitoring;
(2) Ventilation;
(3) Illumination;
(4) Communications;
(5) Flood control;
(6) Mechanical equipment;
(7) Personal protective equipment;
(8) Explosives;
(9) Fire prevention and protection; and
(10) Emergency procedures, including evacuation plans and checkin/check-out systems.
(g) Emergency provisions
(5) Rescue teams.
(iv) On jobsites where flammable or noxious gases are
encountered or anticipated in hazardous quantities, rescue
team members shall practice donning and using selfcontained breathing apparatus monthly.

